<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $4.5 bln in June 30 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $4.5 bln in June 30 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $4.5 billion in the June 30 week to $3,923.8 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $13.0 billion to $5,112.9 billion. M-1 was up $10.1 billion to $1,069.3 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,916.2 billion versus $3,912.6 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
